<title>USA: Shop At Home reaches second carriage pact.</title>
<headline>Shop At Home reaches second carriage pact.</headline>
<dateline>KNOXVILLE, Tenn. 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shop At Home Inc said on Thursday it had reached a second carriage agreement with Multiple Cable System Operator, Tele-Communications Inc (TCI).</p>
<p>Under the terms of the agreement, Shop At Home programming will be launched on no fewer than four million TCI households by November for a minimum of six hours each night, seven nights per week, growing to as many as 10 million households within the first year.</p>
</text>
